/* GENERATED from the `account` federated remote's own icon chunks — regenerate rather than
 * hand-edit; the recipe is at the foot of this file.
 *
 * Twenty-two marks for the six settings panes, all off `hash.game/modules/account/assets/`. Some
 * are their own chunk (`IconSet-BJBHeAWe.js`, `IconEdit-DT-d7sHm.js`, `IconLight-BQc6-mqu.js`, …)
 * and some are inlined in the page chunk that draws them — the rail's Preferences and Whitelist
 * marks in `index-B0Ab1fJ8.js`, the six KYC row marks in `index-DUZ1QIOc.js`, the anti-phishing
 * shield in `index-DnPIrd_m.js`. Both routes end in the same file.
 *
 * THEY CARRY NO `fill` OF THEIR OWN, exactly like the BetBy sprites and the Help Center rail. The
 * original's icon wrapper (`d` in `Wrap-DblNcHvH.js`) prepends `icon` — `fill: currentColor` — to
 * whatever class it is handed, so a call site that forgets a fill gets solid black rather than
 * the row's colour. Every call site here writes `fill-*` or `icon` explicitly.
 *
 * NAMES ARE THIS FILE'S where the remote's would collide with a different drawing already in the
 * project — the `IconInform` / `IconCopy` / Vault Pro trap, which this project has now hit three
 * times. `IconAdd` here is the account remote's plus and is NOT `AfterLogin/icons.jsx`'s;
 * `IconEdit`, `IconDelete` and `IconLink` are likewise the remote's own.
 */

